---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Truth to Live By handles information across its website, newsletter, contact route and owner-operated publishing system."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</span>
      <h1>Privacy, considered.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Clear information about what this website does with your data.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p class="small">Last updated: 1 October 2026.</p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Truth to Live By is an independent publishing project operated by Mark Walsh in Ireland.
        Mark Walsh is the data controller. Privacy questions, requests and concerns can be sent to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${brand.contactEmail}`}>{brand.contactEmail}</a> or through the{' '}
        <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The website and hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This is a static website. It does not create visitor accounts and does not include an
        advertising tracker, analytics service or website contact form. Fonts, thumbnails and
        illustrations are served with the site. The site does not deliberately set cookies or
        local-storage identifiers before a visitor chooses to play a YouTube video.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cloudflare hosts, delivers and protects the website. In doing so, Cloudflare may process
        technical request information such as an IP address, requested URL, date and time, browser
        or device information, and security signals. This processing is necessary to deliver and
        secure the site and supports the legitimate interest in operating a reliable publication.
        Truth to Live By does not currently use Cloudflare Web Analytics or receive individual
        visitor profiles.
      </p>

      <h2>Playing videos</h2>
      <p>
        Before Play is pressed, video thumbnails are served locally and no YouTube player connection
        is made. Pressing Play loads YouTube’s privacy-enhanced player and connects the visitor’s
        browser to YouTube. Google and YouTube can then receive technical and playback information
        and may use browser storage. Privacy-enhanced mode does not make playback anonymous. Closing
        a video removes its player.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        The One Truth to Live By newsletter is provided through beehiiv. Where the embedded signup
        form is enabled, the visitor’s browser may connect to beehiiv as the newsletter section
        approaches the viewport, before an email address is submitted. Beehiiv may then receive
        technical request information such as the visitor’s IP address, browser or device details,
        requested form and referring page. The website does not receive the email address directly.
        Submitting the form sends the address to beehiiv, and Truth to Live By and beehiiv process
        the address, subscription and confirmation status, and the technical, acquisition and
        engagement information that beehiiv records for operating the newsletter. When the embedded
        form is disabled, the newsletter link opens the Truth to Live By publication on beehiiv.
      </p>
      <p>
        Newsletter messages are sent on the basis of consent. A subscriber can withdraw consent at
        any time by using the unsubscribe link in an email or contacting Truth to Live By. Active
        subscriber information is kept while the subscription continues. After unsubscription,
        information is deleted or anonymised when it is no longer needed, except for the minimum
        suppression or compliance record required to honour the unsubscribe request and meet legal
        obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact correspondence</h2>
      <p>
        The Contact page opens the visitor’s email application to write to the dedicated Truth to
        Live By Gmail address. The website does not receive or store the message itself. Google
        processes correspondence sent to that mailbox. Correspondence is used to respond to an
        enquiry, consider a correction or manage a requested professional relationship. The legal
        basis is the legitimate interest in responding and maintaining appropriate records, or steps
        requested before entering an agreement where applicable. Correspondence is normally deleted
        within 24 months after the last substantive contact unless it is still needed for the
        relationship or a legal obligation.
      </p>

      <h2>The owner-operated publishing application</h2>
      <p>
        Truth to Live By uses a private publishing application to manage approved content for its
        official channels. It is not a service offered to website visitors. Its Google OAuth
        connection is authorised by the channel owner and is used to confirm the intended YouTube
        channel, refresh the authorised session and upload owner-selected videos with their titles,
        descriptions and related metadata. This supports the legitimate interest in operating the
        publication securely and preventing uploads to an unexpected channel.
      </p>
      <p>
        The requested Google OAuth permissions are <code>youtube.upload</code>, used to upload the
        owner-selected videos and metadata, and <code>youtube.readonly</code>, used to read the
        authorised channel’s basic identity. The application does not request access to Gmail,
        Google Drive or unrelated Google Account information.
      </p>
      <p>
        For these operations, the application processes the authorised YouTube channel identifier
        and title; OAuth access and refresh credentials; locally selected video files and publishing
        metadata; and the video identifiers, status and operational responses returned by YouTube.
        It does not receive the owner’s Google password.
      </p>
      <p>
        Media and credentials remain in the owner-controlled local publishing environment. They are
        excluded from the website and source repositories. Publishing state and operational logs are
        kept separately for each brand. Google information is used only to provide the requested
        channel-verification and upload functions. It is not sold, used for advertising or shared
        with unrelated third parties.
      </p>
      <p>
        Operational publishing logs are retained for 12 months and then deleted. OAuth credentials
        are retained only while the authorisation remains active and are deleted when they are
        replaced, revoked or no longer required. Access can be revoked through the authorising
        Google Account’s security settings. See <a href="/publishing/">Publishing system</a> for a
        plain-language description of the application.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers and international transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare provides hosting, delivery and security; beehiiv provides the newsletter service;
        and Google provides Gmail and YouTube. These providers may process information outside
        Ireland or the European Economic Area. Where required, transfers are protected through an
        applicable adequacy framework or contractual safeguards such as the European Commission’s
        Standard Contractual Clauses. Each provider also publishes its own privacy information.
      </p>

      <h2>Rights and requests</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on the circumstances, applicable data-protection rights may include access,
        correction, erasure, restriction, objection and portability, along with withdrawal of
        consent and the right to complain to the Irish Data Protection Commission. Send a request to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${brand.contactEmail}`}>{brand.contactEmail}</a>. Identity may need to be
        confirmed before a request is completed. Requests are handled within the legally applicable
        period. Following an approved deletion request, locally stored publishing records are
        deleted within 30 days unless they must be retained to meet a legal obligation.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        This notice will be updated before introducing a new analytics service or other material
        data use. The date above will change when the notice is revised. A cookie-consent interface
        will be added if a future implementation requires one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
